{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואצלתי מן הרוח אשר עליך ושמתי עליהם", :translit "v'atzalti min ha-ruach asher alecha v'samti aleihem", :gloss "and I will take of the spirit that is upon you and put it upon them"} {:he "לא אוכל לשאת משא כל העם הזה", :translit "lo uchal l'seit masa kol ha-am ha-zeh", :gloss "I am not able to bear all this people's burden"} {:he "ויאצל מן הרוח אשר עליו ויתן על שבעים איש", :translit "vayatzal min ha-ruach asher alav vayiten al shiv'im ish", :gloss "and he took of the spirit that was upon him and put it upon the seventy men"} {:he "ותנח עליהם הרוח", :translit "vatanch aleihem ha-ruach", :gloss "and the spirit rested upon them"} {:he "כלאם", :translit "k'laem", :gloss "restrain them"} {:he "מי יתן כל עם ה' נביאים", :translit "mi yiten kol am Hashem n'vi'im", :gloss "would that all the people of Hashem were prophets"} {:he "ונתן עליהם", :translit "v'natan aleihem", :gloss "and gave it upon them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast drawn between ויאצל (he took from) for the seventy elders and ותנח (rested upon) for Eldad and Medad, showing two different sources of prophecy"}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim builds his comment on a close reading of the verbs used for prophecy in Numbers 11. For the seventy elders the verse says ויאצל מן הרוח אשר עליו — Moses took of the spirit that was upon himself — indicating their prophetic spirit was drawn from Moses' own prophecy. But for Eldad and Medad, who were not among the seventy, the verse says ותנח עליהם הרוח — the spirit rested upon them — indicating it came directly from God. This distinction explains Moses' enthusiastic response מי יתן כל עם ה' נביאים (Numbers 11:29): he recognized that Eldad and Medad had received prophecy directly from God rather than being limited to what Moses could impart. The broader narrative context is God's instruction to Moses to gather seventy elders who would share his burden (Numbers 11:16–17), Moses' prior complaint that he could not bear the people alone (Numbers 11:14), and Joshua's request that Moses restrain Eldad and Medad (Numbers 11:28).", :sources ["Numbers 11:14" "Numbers 11:16-17" "Numbers 11:25" "Numbers 11:26" "Numbers 11:28" "Numbers 11:29"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast drawn between ויאצל (he took from) for the seventy elders and ותנח (rested upon) for Eldad and Medad, showing two different sources of prophecy", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:26.012439541Z", :model "glm-5.2"}